{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgfy96PBtfX4rZPDjf3c6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Setup.** Tetrahedral d⁸ has a ³T₁(F) ground state. Its term pattern is the same as octahedral d², so the d² matrices apply with Dq taken as the tetrahedral value. The ³T₂ term does not mix with anything. The ³T₁(F) and ³T₁(P) terms mix through B alone, so C/B = 4.5 has no effect on these two bands.\n\n**Dq from the ³T₂ band.** The ³T₂ level lies at +2Dq and the ³T₁(F) level at −6Dq before mixing. The first band is therefore ν₁ = 8Dq exactly:\n\nDq = 4400 / 8 = 550 cm⁻¹\n\n**B from the ³T₁(P) band.** Take the ³F term at 0 and the ³P term at 15B. The ³T₁ matrix is\n\n[[−6Dq, 4B], [4B, 15B + 6Dq]]\n\nIts eigenvalues are E± = 7.5B ± √[(7.5B + 6Dq)² + 16B²].\n\nThe ground state is E₋, and the upper ³T₁ state is E₊. The second band is ν₃ = E₊ − E₋ = 15 500 cm⁻¹, so\n\n(7.5B + 3300)² + 16B² = 7750² = 60 062 500\n\nThis simplifies to the quadratic 72.25B² + 49 500B − 49 172 500 = 0. Its positive root is B ≈ 551 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 550 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 551 cm⁻¹. This gives C = 4.5B ≈ 2480 cm⁻¹. C was assumed and is not a fitted value.\n\n{\"Dq\": 550, \"B\": 551, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq = ν1/8 from the ³T₂ band, and B from the ³T₁(F)–³T₁(P) 2×2 matrix fitted to 15 500 cm⁻¹.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":845,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":845,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39bf699d-79ea-4e3d-b7d9-a50a53285186","uuid":"3ffa61c0-55e2-432b-b8a2-762bf07808cf","timestamp":"2026-11-03T12:08:57.756Z","request_id":"req_011Cgfy964bBCNC19mQt